1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,098
A product catalog lists products that visitors can browse by category and find with search.

2
00:00:07,098 --> 00:00:11,688
In this video, you build one in Orchard Core, with content types, a

3
00:00:11,688 --> 00:00:14,580
taxonomy, the Media Library, and Search.

4
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:21,619
Every product has the same structure:

5
00:00:21,619 --> 00:00:24,398
a name, a price, a picture, and a category.

6
00:00:24,398 --> 00:00:29,105
A content type defines that structure, and the Content Types feature lets you

7
00:00:29,105 --> 00:00:30,750
build one in the admin.

8
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:36,040
A taxonomy holds the categories, and the Taxonomies feature manages it.

9
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:41,700
The Media feature stores the pictures in the Media Library, so every product can show one.

10
00:00:42,450 --> 00:00:46,936
The Search feature adds a search page, which finds products in an index.

11
00:00:46,936 --> 00:00:52,170
You build the types, the categories, the pictures, the products, and then the search.

12
00:00:56,470 --> 00:00:58,598
Let's start with the Product type.

13
00:00:58,598 --> 00:01:03,120
Under Design, Content Definition, Content Types, you see the types of the site.

14
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:04,610
Click Create new type.

15
00:01:05,084 --> 00:01:07,527
Enter Product as the Display Name.

16
00:01:07,527 --> 00:01:10,214
The Technical Name fills in by itself.

17
00:01:10,214 --> 00:01:11,374
Click Create.

18
00:01:11,837 --> 00:01:13,663
A type is made of parts.

19
00:01:13,663 --> 00:01:19,327
The Title part gives every product a name, so check Title and click Add Selected Parts.

20
00:01:19,782 --> 00:01:24,138
The Parts list shows Product, the part that holds the fields of this type.

21
00:01:24,138 --> 00:01:26,644
A field stores a value, such as a price.

22
00:01:26,644 --> 00:01:27,842
Click Add Field.

23
00:01:28,295 --> 00:01:34,055
Enter Price as the Display Name, choose Numeric Field, and click Save & Configure.

24
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:38,387
Set Scale to 2, so a price has two digits after the decimal

25
00:01:38,387 --> 00:01:40,291
point, and check Required.

26
00:01:40,291 --> 00:01:41,600
Then click Save.

27
00:01:42,068 --> 00:01:43,651
Add a second field.

28
00:01:43,651 --> 00:01:47,198
Name it Image, choose Media Field, and click Save.

29
00:01:47,198 --> 00:01:50,808
By default, a Media Field accepts several pictures.

30
00:01:51,271 --> 00:01:53,823
The type lists its fields and its parts.

31
00:01:53,823 --> 00:01:56,931
Click Save to return to the list of content types.

32
00:01:58,631 --> 00:02:03,226
Categories are content items too, so each one needs a content type.

33
00:02:03,226 --> 00:02:08,011
Click Create new type, and enter Product Category as the Display Name.

34
00:02:08,482 --> 00:02:12,553
Click Create, check Title, and click Add Selected Parts.

35
00:02:12,553 --> 00:02:15,902
A category only needs a title, so click Save.

36
00:02:20,202 --> 00:02:23,832
A taxonomy holds the categories, as terms.

37
00:02:23,832 --> 00:02:28,822
Open Content, Content Items, click New, and choose Taxonomy.

38
00:02:29,330 --> 00:02:31,867
Enter Product Categories as the Title.

39
00:02:31,867 --> 00:02:36,767
For Term Content Type, choose Product Category, which is the type of each term.

40
00:02:36,767 --> 00:02:37,920
Click Publish.

41
00:02:38,386 --> 00:02:41,013
Open the taxonomy again with Edit.

42
00:02:41,013 --> 00:02:45,806
The Add Product Category button appears once the taxonomy is saved.

43
00:02:46,270 --> 00:02:51,570
Click Add Product Category, enter Backpacks as the Title, and click Publish.

44
00:02:51,570 --> 00:02:54,090
The term appears in the taxonomy.

45
00:02:54,559 --> 00:02:57,352
Add Tents and Sleeping Bags the same way.

46
00:02:57,352 --> 00:03:01,689
A term also has an Add button, which creates a child term below it.

47
00:03:12,684 --> 00:03:15,840
The terms are saved in a draft of the taxonomy.

48
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:19,354
Click Publish to publish the taxonomy with its terms.

49
00:03:21,054 --> 00:03:24,399
Next, connect the Product type to the taxonomy.

50
00:03:24,399 --> 00:03:28,754
Open Content Types, click Edit on Product, and click Add Field.

51
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:35,709
Enter Category as the Display Name, choose Taxonomy Field, and click Save & Configure.

52
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:39,306
Select Product Categories as the Taxonomy.

53
00:03:39,306 --> 00:03:43,960
Check Unique, so a product has only one category, and click Save.

54
00:03:44,412 --> 00:03:46,776
The Product type has three fields:

55
00:03:46,776 --> 00:03:48,726
Price, Image, and Category.

56
00:03:48,726 --> 00:03:51,562
Each field is saved as soon as you add it.

57
00:03:55,862 --> 00:03:59,132
Product pictures belong in the Media Library.

58
00:03:59,132 --> 00:04:03,684
Open Tools, Features, search for Media Slugify, and click Enable.

59
00:04:03,684 --> 00:04:09,902
It gives uploaded files and folders web-friendly names, and leaves existing ones unchanged.

60
00:04:11,602 --> 00:04:13,195
Open Media, Library.

61
00:04:13,195 --> 00:04:16,320
The folder tree starts with the Files folder.

62
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:19,812
Use its folder menu, and choose Create a subfolder.

63
00:04:20,269 --> 00:04:24,563
Enter Product Photos as the folder name, and click Ok.

64
00:04:24,563 --> 00:04:28,499
Media Slugify turns the name into product-photos.

65
00:04:28,957 --> 00:04:32,162
Select the folder, and click Upload files.

66
00:04:32,162 --> 00:04:34,966
Choose the pictures of the products.

67
00:04:34,966 --> 00:04:40,307
Media Slugify renames each file, so Trail Backpack becomes trail-backpack.

68
00:04:44,607 --> 00:04:48,963
Open Content, Content Items, click New, and choose Product.

69
00:04:48,963 --> 00:04:54,927
The editor shows the Title, and a field for the price, the image, and the category.

70
00:04:55,379 --> 00:04:59,819
Enter Trail Backpack as the Title, and 89 as the Price.

71
00:05:01,855 --> 00:05:03,782
For Image, click Add media.

72
00:05:03,782 --> 00:05:06,234
The Media Library opens in a window.

73
00:05:06,234 --> 00:05:10,205
Select the picture in the product-photos folder, and click OK.

74
00:05:11,424 --> 00:05:16,244
For Category, choose Backpacks, one of the terms you added to the taxonomy.

75
00:05:16,819 --> 00:05:21,291
The Save Draft button keeps a product unpublished, and with the default index

76
00:05:21,291 --> 00:05:23,715
settings, search does not find a draft.

77
00:05:23,715 --> 00:05:25,223
Click Publish instead.

78
00:05:25,223 --> 00:05:28,509
A message confirms that the product has been published.

79
00:05:29,031 --> 00:05:31,285
Add the other products the same way.

80
00:05:31,285 --> 00:05:34,291
The list of content items shows the whole catalog.

81
00:05:38,491 --> 00:05:42,114
An index lists the words of your content, and each word points to

82
00:05:42,114 --> 00:05:44,155
the content items that contain it.

83
00:05:44,155 --> 00:05:46,911
The search page looks the words up in the index.

84
00:05:47,661 --> 00:05:49,620
Search needs three steps.

85
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:54,170
Create an index, choose it as the default search index in the site

86
00:05:54,170 --> 00:05:57,141
settings, and allow visitors to query it.

87
00:05:57,891 --> 00:06:02,351
When a visitor searches, the page checks the permission, looks the words up

88
00:06:02,351 --> 00:06:05,931
in the default index, and shows each matching content item.

89
00:06:07,631 --> 00:06:11,976
Lucene builds the index, and Search adds the search page.

90
00:06:11,976 --> 00:06:16,391
Open Tools, Features, search for Lucene, and click Enable.

91
00:06:16,841 --> 00:06:19,401
Then enable the feature named Search.

92
00:06:19,401 --> 00:06:24,401
Both features depend on the Indexing feature, which provides index management.

93
00:06:26,101 --> 00:06:29,368
Open Search, Indexes, and click Add index.

94
00:06:29,368 --> 00:06:35,561
In the list of sources, click Add for Content in Lucene, which indexes content items.

95
00:06:36,023 --> 00:06:38,306
Enter products as the Index Name.

96
00:06:38,306 --> 00:06:41,642
Under Content types, check Product, and click Save.

97
00:06:41,642 --> 00:06:44,803
By default, only published versions are indexed.

98
00:06:45,259 --> 00:06:49,616
The index appears in the list, and Orchard Core builds it in the background.

99
00:06:49,616 --> 00:06:52,219
Products you publish later are added to it.

100
00:06:53,919 --> 00:06:57,274
Next, tell the search page which index to use.

101
00:06:57,274 --> 00:06:59,919
Open Settings, Search, Site Search.

102
00:07:00,390 --> 00:07:05,895
Choose products as the Default search index, and enter Search products as the Placeholder.

103
00:07:05,895 --> 00:07:06,870
Click Save.

104
00:07:08,570 --> 00:07:12,320
Visitors who are not signed in need permission to search.

105
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:16,010
Open Access Control, Roles, and click Edit on Anonymous.

106
00:07:16,626 --> 00:07:21,472
Type products in Search permissions, and allow Query 'products' Index.

107
00:07:21,472 --> 00:07:22,556
Click Save.

108
00:07:24,256 --> 00:07:28,330
Open the search page of the site, at the address /search.

109
00:07:28,330 --> 00:07:30,786
Type backpack, and click Search.

110
00:07:31,270 --> 00:07:36,001
The result shows the product with its title, price, picture, and category.

111
00:07:36,001 --> 00:07:38,780
Click the title to open the product page.

112
00:07:39,247 --> 00:07:43,332
The product page shows the price, the picture, and the category.

113
00:07:43,332 --> 00:07:46,307
A visitor reaches it from the search results.

114
00:07:46,761 --> 00:07:50,369
A word that no product contains shows a message instead:

115
00:07:50,369 --> 00:07:52,231
There are no such results.

116
00:07:56,431 --> 00:08:01,438
A content type defines the products, a taxonomy groups them, the Media Library

117
00:08:01,438 --> 00:08:04,478
stores their pictures, and Search finds them.

118
00:08:04,478 --> 00:08:07,041
You configure each part in the admin.

119
00:08:09,041 --> 00:08:15,003
You built a product catalog with a content type, a taxonomy, the Media Library, and Search.

120
00:08:15,003 --> 00:08:16,601
Thanks for watching.

